1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,200
What was that?

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,500
Just the shutter. Did you think
someone was at the door?

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,500
In this weather? Nobody's out tonight.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,300
The dog didn't even lift her head.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
She's slept through worse, apparently.
That's what the note says.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
They left a note? Three pages,
front and back.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,200
Feed at six. Walk before the rain.
Insulin at seven, with her dinner.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,500
Insulin? Nobody told me about insulin.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,700
I've never given an injection in my life.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,400
It's a tiny needle. She won't mind.

11
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,500
You're saying that because
you're not the one doing it.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,200
Did we walk her before the rain?

13
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,500
We walked her. She did nothing
and then sat in a puddle.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,500
She needs a bath, but a towel will do.

15
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Towels are in the hall cupboard,
second shelf.

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,100
Come here. Come on, good girl.

17
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,200
She's shaking water all over me.
That's her way of saying thank you.

18
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,900
The rain's getting heavier.

19
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,600
The note says the power goes out
when it storms like this.

20
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,200
There are candles in the kitchen drawer
and a torch by the back door.

21
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,800
I'll find the torch.
You start her dinner.

22
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,200
Found it. The batteries are flat,
but there are spares in the drawer.

23
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,200
Dinner's ready. She's already
sitting by her bowl.

24
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,700
Then it's seven. Time for the injection.

25
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,600
Pinch the skin at the back of her neck
into a little tent.

26
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,800
Perfect. Now the needle goes in
under the skin, nearly flat.

27
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,300
She's eating. She hasn't noticed.

28
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,800
Push the plunger. Slowly.

29
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,100
Done. Needle out. Cap back on.

30
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,300
Told you. She didn't flinch once.

31
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,300
I flinched enough for both of us.

32
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,100
The needle goes in the sharps box
on the counter.

33
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,600
Listen to that wind.

34
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,700
The trees out back are bending
half over.

35
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,900
Leave the curtains open.
I like watching it.

36
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,200
Whoa. That lightning was close.

37
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,900
The lights are flickering.

38
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,500
If the flashing bothers you,
look away from the window.

39
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
The window! It's blown open!

40
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Help me shut it. Push harder.

41
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,400
Got it. Latch it.

42
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:05,000
The lights have stopped flickering.
They've gone out completely.

43
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,700
Where's the torch? Wait,
where's the dog?

44
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,200
She was right here a second ago.

45
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:23,200
Check under the table. That's where
she hides, according to the note.

46
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,500
Can you hear that? Something rattling.

47
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,700
That's her collar. She's in the kitchen.

48
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
There you are. You scared me.

49
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:49,400
She's fine. She was finishing
her dinner in the dark.

50
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,800
Let's light some candles.

51
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:11,300
Candles are on the table.
Matches are in my pocket.

52
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,400
It's actually quite nice like this.

53
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,900
Until the ice cream melts.

54
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:34,400
There's ice cream? Then we should
probably eat it now.

55
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,200
Fair point. I'll get the bowls.

56
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,100
What broke?

57
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:50,600
A glass fell off the counter.
Don't come in here barefoot.

58
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,500
Oh no. She's walked right through it.

59
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,800
She's limping. Her paw's bleeding a little.

60
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,500
Bring the candle closer.
Let me look.

61
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,800
There's a small piece of glass in her pad.

62
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,200
It's out. It's only a small cut.

63
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,300
Poor thing. She's licking my hand.

64
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:33,200
The note has a number for the vet
in an emergency.

65
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:42,400
It's not an emergency.
The bleeding's already stopped.

66
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:48,000
I'll clean it and wrap it.
The first aid kit is in the bathroom.

67
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,100
Gauze and tape. Not too tight?

68
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:02,000
You should be able to slide
a finger under it.

69
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,900
Perfect. She looks very proud
of her bandage.

70
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:17,400
I'll sweep up the glass
before anything else happens.

71
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,300
I'll keep her on the sofa with me.

72
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,600
She's asleep already.

73
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:43,800
I'll message the owners to say she's fine.

74
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:52,100
Tell them about the paw too.
They'd want to know.

75
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,900
The power's coming back on.

76
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,300
They're flickering again. Hang on.

77
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,900
I almost miss the candles.

78
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:18,500
Blow them out before the dog
wakes up and investigates.

79
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,700
The storm's moving off.

80
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,700
Not a bad first night.

81
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:37,900
Not bad? The window, the glass,
the needle...

82
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,600
And nobody panicked.

83
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,400
Same time tomorrow for her insulin?

84
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:58,400
Seven o'clock. This time
I'll do the needle on my own.
